# Shell wait

Start a long repository command with `block_until_ms: 0`. Continue other work. The completion notice is the end signal.

Poll with AwaitShell only when the next step is blocked on that process. Wait for process exit. A pattern is valid only when that line cannot appear before the command ends.

A successful complete `make verify` prints `verified parent #100` after the last tracker check. A successful `make verify-local` ends with the line `verified <n> transaction-control statements on PooledClient receivers`; in a complete `make verify` that line appears before the tracker check and is not the end. A failed make target may print `make: *** [verify`.

These strings are not AwaitShell patterns:

- `verify-stage1` is the contracts self-check. It can appear near 15 seconds.
- `Error:` is an expected Storage Activation reject (`MissingOrInactive` / `IdentityMismatch`).

Set the poll window from the command class:

| Command | Typical duration |
|---|---|
| GitHub PR `verify` sentinel | about 16 seconds |
| Dirty-tree `make verify` | fails in about 24 seconds |
| Clean complete `make verify-local` | about 2.5 minutes |
| One `verify-tracker` | tens of seconds |
| Clean complete `make verify` | about 3 minutes |

When a poll is required for a clean complete `make verify`, wait for process exit. Treat `verified parent #100` as the success line. Do not open a second long wait after a mid-run line.
